    <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-01-01">1 January 2026</time> · 1 min read</p>
    <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Tags">
  <li><a href="/tags/meta/" rel="tag">meta</a></li>
</ul>

  </header>
  <div class="prose">
<p>This Post is Markdown. Its math is LaTeX, which becomes MathML when the Site is built, so no script draws it.</p>
<h2 id="an-equation">An equation</h2>
<p>The sum of the first <math><mi>n</mi></math> odd numbers is a square:</p>
<math display="block"><mtable displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0" style="width: 100%"><mtr><mtd style="width: 50%"></mtd><mtd><munderover><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd style="width: 50%;text-align: right;justify-items: end;" id="eq:odd"><mtext>(1)</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>
<h2 id="a-theorem">A theorem</h2>
<div class="theorem" data-kind="theorem" id="thm:gauss">
<p><span class="theorem-head"><span class="theorem-name">Theorem 1</span> <span class="theorem-title">(Gauss)</span>.</span> For every <math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, <math><munderover><mo lspace="0">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, and so <a href="#eq:odd">(1)</a> holds.</p>
</div>
<div class="proof">
<p><span class="proof-head">Proof.</span> Each <math><mi>k</mi></math> pairs with <math><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, and the <math><mi>n</mi></math> pairs, which count the sum twice, each add up to <math><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then the odd numbers sum to <math><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.2222em" rspace="0.2222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0" rspace="0">+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. <span class="qed" role="img" aria-label="End of proof">∎</span></p>
</div>
<p>A link with no text to a Label shows its number, as <a href="#eq:odd">(1)</a> and <a href="#thm:gauss">Theorem 1</a> do here. In Org, <code>\eqref</code> in prose does the same.</p>
<h2 id="some-code">Some code</h2>
<pre class="y-code" tabindex="0" data-language="rust"><code><span class="ji">fn </span><span class="cb11">odd_sum</span><span class="id">(</span><span class="ok">n</span><span class="be">: </span><span class="ji">u64</span><span class="id">) </span><span class="be">-> </span><span class="ji">u64 </span><span class="id">{</span>
    <span class="id">(</span><span class="qq">1</span><span class="be">..=</span>n<span class="id">)</span><span class="be">.</span><span class="cb11">map</span><span class="id">(</span><span class="be">|</span>k<span class="be">| </span><span class="qq">2 </span><span class="be">* </span>k <span class="be">- </span><span class="qq">1</span><span class="id">)</span><span class="be">.</span><span class="cb11">sum</span><span class="id">()</span>
<span class="id">}</span></code></pre>
<p><code>hello-org.org</code> says the same in Org.</p>
  </div>
</article>
<p class="visually-hidden" role="status" data-code-copy="Copy" data-copied="Copied"></p>

</main>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <p>&copy; Your Name. <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a></p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
